# Soma Messages linked to the Mac's iMessage service (0.6+). Against the service's DEMO on the Mac Pro: sample
# chats only, nothing of Boss's; every send gets a fake reply 2 s later. The token below is the demo's own.
shell cmd statusbar collapse
key HOME
# A clean start: not linked yet, no contacts answer.
shell pm clear dev.omalauncher.messages
# Contacts allowed ahead, so Android's prompt (whose title also says Allow) doesn't cover the inbox.
shell pm grant dev.omalauncher.messages android.permission.READ_CONTACTS
# 0.7+ asks for notifications when linked; granted here so its prompt does not cover the inbox.
shell pm grant dev.omalauncher.messages android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS
# Quoted twice: walk.py hands the line to the phone's shell, which would split the link at '&'.
shell am start -a android.intent.action.VIEW -d "'soma-messages://link?url=http%3A%2F%2F100.120.219.46%3A8765&token=BON7avwraojOZCR1WT8sLWZg9WTx0RFaqeR3udg1kzA'" dev.omalauncher.messages
wait 2500
# The owner says yes to the Mac by name before anything goes to it.
expect Get your iMessages from 100.120.219.46?
shot link-dialog
tap Link
wait 1500
# Names come from the phone's contacts; the Mac's names stand in when the phone has none.
wait 4000
expect Weekend
expect Ana Demo
absent OpenBubbles
shot inbox-from-the-mac
tap Weekend
wait 2000
expect Look at this
# The photo itself, fetched from the Mac (the demo's is a tiny orange square), in place of a "1 Photo" card.
expect Photo
# Not a sliver: the photo fills a 240 dp frame (the demo's 2x2 picture scaled up to an orange block).
shot photo-fills-its-frame
expect from your Mac
shot group-with-photo-card
key BACK
wait 800
tap Ana Demo
wait 2000
# A threaded reply from the Mac shows the message it answers.
# The demo keeps every test message, so the older reply sits above them: scroll back up to it.
# The demo keeps every walk's messages, so the history grows: far enough up for many runs.
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 400
wait 600
expect Perfect, see you there
expect You: Yes! 7pm
# Ana's love tapback on "Yes! 7pm" (the demo's own), under that message.
expect ❤️
shot reply-quote
# Back down before writing, so the answer shows. Swiped, not "tap Latest": a short demo thread is all on one
# screen, and the pill only shows once scrolled away from the bottom (the 0.7.6 walk failed on it).
swipe 0.5 0.8 0.5 0.3 200
swipe 0.5 0.8 0.5 0.3 200
swipe 0.5 0.8 0.5 0.3 200
wait 800
# The field and the send button by place (cover screen): "Message" would also match the inbox's heading, under
# the conversation.
tap 0.5 0.925
wait 600
type walk test from the Fold
wait 600
shot typed
# With words in the field, the arrow is the send button, and says so (TalkBack reads it too).
expect Send
# A hardware Enter sends (the on-screen Return breaks the line, as Apple's does); the keyboard moves the arrow.
key ENTER
wait 1500
# Only a message that went gets an answer: the demo replies to each send 2 s later. (The draft in the field would
# match the sent words too, so they prove nothing.)
wait 3000
expect Demo reply to: walk test from the Fold
shot sent-and-answered
# Videos (0.7.7; Boss's phone, 2026-10-23: "1 Video" did nothing). The demo's "Clips" chat has one short MP4 from the
# other person. Not fetched until tapped; then it plays in the phone's player, and is shown by a frame of its own.
# Back twice: the first only puts the keyboard away after the send; the second leaves Ana's chat for the inbox.
key BACK
wait 600
key BACK
wait 800
expect Clips
tap Clips
wait 1500
expect Tap to play
tap Tap to play
wait 5000
shot video-playing
# Back from the player to the chat: the app brought forward, as the number of Backs the player takes varies (the
# emulator's first full-screen sheet took one of its own).
key BACK
wait 800
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.messages/.MainActivity
wait 1500
expect Video, tap to play
absent Getting it from your Mac
# Look: the video shown by a frame from it, with a play mark.
shot video-frame
# Held, the video's frame opens the same menu as words: tapbacks, Reply (0.7.8; Boss, 2026-10-23: tapbacks didn't
# work on pictures, as the picture's own tap took the hold). A long press on the frame, by place (cover, 0.29 down).
swipe 0.3 0.29 0.3 0.29 900
wait 800
expect Reply
shot hold-menu-on-video
# Back closes the menu only: the chat stays, and its link still opens after (the 0.7.8 walk: it didn't).
key BACK
wait 600
absent Copy
expect Clips
# A shared link (the demo's second "Clips" message, "https://www.tiktok.com/@soma/video/1"): a card, and a tap opens it.
expect tiktok.com
tap tiktok.com
wait 4000
shot link-opened
key BACK
wait 1000
expect Clips
# Unfolded, the side panel's "Photos & files": the video plays from there too (it said "Open in OpenBubbles" and did
# nothing once linked to the Mac).
fold open
wait 2500
expect Photos & files
# The panel's card by its title: "Tap to play" also matches the chat's video ("Video, tap to play"; matching ignores case).
tap 1 Video
wait 7000
shot panel-video-playing
# Back to the app as after the first video: the player's full-screen sheet takes a Back of its own.
shell am start -W -n dev.omalauncher.messages/.MainActivity
wait 1000
fold folded
wait 2500
# Older history (0.7.6): the demo's "Long thread" has 120 messages, "Long #1" (the oldest, "Long thread starts here")
# to "Long #120"; the first fetch brings 50, the demo's earlier pages fewer, so scrolling to the top loads several.
# From Clips (no keyboard up): one Back to the inbox.
key BACK
wait 800
expect Long thread
tap Long thread
wait 1500
expect Long #120
absent Long #60
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
wait 400
swipe 0.5 0.3 0.5 0.85 300
