wait 2000
expect Long thread starts here
# Look: oldest first at the top, no message twice across the pages' seams (#70/#71, #20/#21), no jump.
shot long-thread-top
# At the side: the middle of the bottom is where the Latest pill sits.
swipe 0.2 0.85 0.2 0.3 300
wait 600
# No "new" count for history loaded above (0.7.7 walk: "↓ 36 new" after paging).
absent new
shot long-thread-seam
# The Mac stopped: the inbox says so and keeps what it has.
[phone] With the real service on the MacBook: link from the phone-link file (Taildropped), chats and names are Boss's own, one plain-text send to a chat he picks arrives on his other devices, a reply from him shows within seconds.
[phone] Mac locked: one plain text and one tapback (later slice) still go; note which don't.
[phone] Hold a message from someone: the six tapbacks show above Reply/Copy; tapping one puts it under the message here and on the Mac; tapping it again takes it off.
[phone] Open a long chat with a friend and scroll to the top: older messages keep coming past the first 50, in order, with nothing twice.
[phone] With the Mac asleep (lid closed), send a message: one "Not sent" line under it, and an error bar under the conversation that goes by itself after a few seconds and isn't shown in other conversations. Wake the Mac: if the message went after all, its "Not sent" goes; a new send there clears any error left.
[phone] Tap a video a friend sent: it comes from the Mac (a moment), plays in the phone's player with sound, and Back returns to the chat, where the video now shows a frame of itself.
[phone] Tap a TikTok or Instagram link a friend sent: it opens (in TikTok/Instagram, or beside the chat on the open Fold), and Back returns to the chat.
[phone] Hold a photo a friend sent: the tapback picker shows; pick one: it shows under the photo here and on the Mac.
[phone] Open the chat with the friend's voice message: it shows as "Voice message · Tap to play"; a tap plays it here, in the conversation, with sound; a second tap stops it. A PDF or document a friend sent says "Tap to open" and opens in the app for it.
[phone] Play a video, close Soma Messages from recents, open the chat again: the video still shows its own frame, not the plain card.
